WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.325
This is just a skill video on how to take notes in our course.

00:00:05.375 --> 00:00:09.387
So anytime you come across an assignment that says, Watch and take notes.

00:00:09.438 --> 00:00:13.450
You should be expecting that you are going to be watching a video,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.950
and you are going to be writing down

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.080
pieces of information to help. You understand a concept.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:23.950
Okay, so the easiest way to take notes in this class is going to

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.385
be using this annotation tool right here.

00:00:26.435 --> 00:00:30.559
Okay, I do give you some other options that we'll talk about.

00:00:30.609 --> 00:00:34.385
But I'm just going to talk about the easiest one first.

00:00:34.435 --> 00:00:39.950
So what you want to do is you actually want to open this whole assignment up

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.266
in a separate tab. So we're going to double open this assignment.

00:00:43.316 --> 00:00:46.582
So the way I do that is, I come to the top,

00:00:46.632 --> 00:00:48.792
and I'm just going to duplicate my tab.

00:00:48.842 --> 00:00:52.661
So I right clicked it, and I was able to go in and just

00:00:52.711 --> 00:00:55.700
click duplicate. And now I have 2 of the same tab.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:59.568
So I'm going to have my video in one and then in the other.

00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:00.950
I'm going to click annotation.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.550
So down here I have my annotation, and I'm going to now click on

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.950
that tab and drag it out

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.950
right here.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.138
Next, I want to make my screen.

00:01:12.188 --> 00:01:14.950
Go to one side and it's called split screen.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.325
I have a setting where I can just do some things on my keyboard

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:22.450
to make it go to the right and the left,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.825
you likely will just hover over the top, and there will be options to

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:29.950
have it go to the right or to the left.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.164
and if you have trouble finding those, come, see me,

00:01:33.214 --> 00:01:37.343
and I will help you. It's the easiest way to split your screen,

00:01:37.393 --> 00:01:41.843
so you can kind of maximize your space next, you probably want to minimize

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:46.343
these little tabs because you probably have a smaller screen that you're working with.

00:01:46.393 --> 00:01:47.950
So just minimize those tabs.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.984
And then we have our video in one tab over here.

00:01:51.034 --> 00:01:54.571
You don't want to go into full screen, because if you do that,

00:01:54.621 --> 00:01:58.433
then it'll just disappear, or the rest of this that we have going on.

00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:01.467
But you could always zoom it in if you need to,

00:02:01.517 --> 00:02:03.950
so you could make your screen actually bigger itself.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.178
Okay? And then, as you are watching, you are going to.

00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:11.287
And I'm going to actually turn off my voice over here as you are

00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:14.222
watching, you are going to be taking notes over here.

00:02:14.272 --> 00:02:18.330
You just click that little t toolbar, and you just drop a text in

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:22.439
wherever you need it. And so, as you're watching, you will be listening to

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:26.548
what I am saying over here, and then it also will help you fill

00:02:26.598 --> 00:02:30.950
in your notes over here. So homeostasis is the need of an organism to stay.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:39.950
And we have stable by regulating its internal conditions.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.850
Okay? And then you just keep going all the way through as you're listening,

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:48.350
and so you'll find that you're able to just press,

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.550
play, and press, pause, and continue typing in your responses over here.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.950
Once you have finished.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.371
you go ahead and click, submit assignment at the bottom,

00:02:57.421 --> 00:03:00.792
and it will. I'll just go ahead and show you.

00:03:00.842 --> 00:03:04.555
So make sure you finish all the way to the bottom.

00:03:04.605 --> 00:03:06.950
You go ahead and click, submit assignment.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.950
and it'll show you your notes with all of your added in notes.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:15.853
Okay, if you want to house these all in one area.

00:03:15.903 --> 00:03:18.492
So you're able to look back at them later on,

00:03:18.542 --> 00:03:22.186
you could just click that download, and you could save them all to one

00:03:22.236 --> 00:03:25.881
file in your on your computer or save them to all one file in

00:03:25.931 --> 00:03:29.575
your Google drive. So if you want all of your notes in one spot.

00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.950
That would be a great way of doing that.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.338
the next option would be to take notes in a physical notebook.

00:03:35.388 --> 00:03:38.726
Okay, so if you choose to do this, what I mean is,

00:03:38.776 --> 00:03:42.679
you have a notebook at home that you are going to handwrite out your

00:03:42.729 --> 00:03:45.503
notes after you do that if you choose this option.

00:03:45.553 --> 00:03:49.174
I also recommend using the Canvas student app instead of using your computer.

00:03:49.224 --> 00:03:53.126
If you use your computer, you're going to be taking notes and holding them

00:03:53.176 --> 00:03:55.950
up to a webcam, and that will be blurry and

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.998
cumbersome, and just kind of a little more complicated.

00:03:59.048 --> 00:04:03.402
So if you do have the Canvas or you do have a phone,

00:04:03.452 --> 00:04:08.144
you can download the Canvas student app, and you can upload those notes right

00:04:08.194 --> 00:04:12.885
here. So you would just take a picture within your phone and then you

00:04:12.935 --> 00:04:16.950
would upload them in to right here to share your notes. Okay.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.950
a 3rd option that some students do is they

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.950
take and they download the PDF itself.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.184
and they put it in another format.

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:32.652
So some people don't like working within annotations, but they prefer working in some

00:04:32.702 --> 00:04:36.482
other format, like maybe Adobe or something, and that's fine as well,

00:04:36.532 --> 00:04:40.950
or you could. If you have the option, you could download these notes printed.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.318
and then take notes and upload them.

00:04:43.368 --> 00:04:47.040
So there are quite a few different ways of doing notes.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:51.439
But, like I said, the easiest option will be annotations directly in Canvas.

00:04:51.489 --> 00:04:54.822
So if you need any help as you're working through,

00:04:54.872 --> 00:04:58.206
please reach out. And if you do take digital notes,

00:04:58.256 --> 00:05:00.236
I should have said this earlier.

00:05:00.286 --> 00:05:04.973
But if you do take digital notes, please make sure that you do put

00:05:05.023 --> 00:05:09.710
whatever the class name is, your assignment title, and your name at the top.
